#META 2026-11-24^November 20, 2026^May 2026 to October 2026 ¶ #NOTE 0~Employment-based Form I-485 petitions are generally adjudicated by USCIS’ Field Office Directorate. To find processing times for employment-based Forms I-485 in the first (EB-1), second (EB-2), and third (EB-3) preference categories, use the filters for field office locations. The processing times listed for Service Center Operations are only for fourth preference (EB-4) and fifth preference (EB-5) Form I-485 employment-based cases. The processing times shown on the website do not include visa-regressed adjustment applications. If an applicant's priority date is not earlier than the applicable visa available cut-off date published in the Visa Bulletin (available at travel.state.gov), we cannot approve their adjustment of status application until a visa is available to them based on their priority date, preference category, and country of chargeability. ¶ #NOTE 1~$2 ¶ #NOTE 2~The Service Center Operations Directorate no longer receives Form I-485 applications based on a grant of asylum status. As of Sept. 28, 2020, the Field Operations Directorate receives all Form I-485 applications based on a grant of asylum status. If you have a case filed before that time that a service center is working on, you may ask for more information through the USCIS eRequest Service Tool online (egov.uscis.gov/e-request/Intro.do) or by calling the USCIS Contact Center. ¶ #NOTE 3~The Service Center Operations Directorate no longer receives Form I-485 applications based on a grant of refugee status. As of Sept. 28, 2020, the Field Operations Directorate receives all Form I-485 applications based on a grant of refugee status. If you have a case filed before that time that a service center is working on, you may ask for more information through the USCIS eRequest Service Tool online (egov.uscis.gov/e-request/Intro.do) or by calling the USCIS Contact Center. ¶ #OFF SCD~Service Center Operations (SCOPS) ¶ #OFF FOD~All Field 